WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.580
This month's sales ranking
(Literature dept)
1. "The box that houses the moon"
Akihiko Usami

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.150
2. "Nostalgia for the 25th century"
Akihiko Usami
3. "All of Japan's inverted
pandas in pictures"
Akihiko Usami

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.900
Yes!

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.880
4. "Scare crow"
Akihiko Usami

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.490
All the books I worked on are best sellers!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.460
Like this one...and this one!

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.870
All my hard work paid off!

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.040
Huh?

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.040
Wait! These are girl comics...

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:26.750
Hey.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.340
Takano?

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.300
Hey...  huh?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.420
Oh my god!

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.400
It was just a dream!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.040
This sucks.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:17.510
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:17.510
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.060
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.060
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.690
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.690
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.480
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.480
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.490
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.490
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.330
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.330
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:46.710
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:46.710
If I reach out my hand

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.080
hajimete no kimochi

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.080
Will you understand my feelings?

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:53.460
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:53.460
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.840
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.840
I love you more and more every second

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.970
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.970
We're still far from a happy ending

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:12.940
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:12.940
But I want to make it come true

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.400
tsuzuite yuku

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.400
Our story continues

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.720
What?!

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.050
It's not done?!

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.230
Why not?!

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.130
Who was it that said yesterday
that it would be done this morning?

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.300
Then when?

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.460
What?! You don't know?!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.730
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.730
I see...

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.140
So this is hell week.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.120
Gloom

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.540
What the fuck?!

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.800
Do you know how much shit we had to go through...

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.930
...with the printer to get an extension?!

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.640
Excuse me?!

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.800
Just shut up and get to
writing that manuscript already.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.770
Onodera, come on.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.270
We're gonna pay this writer-clown a visit.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.270
You mean we're going now?

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.590
We'll paste in the photo typeset
there and grab the last twelve pages.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.740
And bring your X-Acto knife.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.680
You'll end up pasting in the toner, too.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.080
Uh, but I don't have the right skill set for...

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.480
Well, you're the only one doing jack right now.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.000
I'm counting on you guys.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.560
Hello, yes, this is Takano
from Marukawa Publishing.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.500
May I speak to Sasaki please?

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.480
So what, now I'm just supposed
to go to this author's house?

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.810
I've never even helped out with a manga before.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.090
I can't do this...

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.490
I'm probably just getting in the way.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.140
Hello, Sasaki?

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.320
I'm very sorry, but I can't make it today.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.820
I know that!

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.530
Yes, all right.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.240
Yes.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:52.410
Who is Takano talking to?

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.330
Could he be talking to the author again?

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.590
That's why I'm asking you to do something!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.330
Why is he so restless?

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.680
And why...

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:14.970
...does everyone in the manga
business look so lifeless?!

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.690
T-Takano...

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.450
If you feel guilty enough to
cry, get it done on time!

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.450
I can't do it and that's that!

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.570
How dare you talk back to me?!

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:28.950
I will strike you where you stand!

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.510
And besides, why the hell are you
drawing the Nikkō Tōshō-gū...

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.330
...on the first page when you're so behind?!

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.210
It's better than the Sanjūsangendō!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.210
Shut up and just get back to work!

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.710
I know I'm causing you trouble,

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:54.050
but this page will be a featured spread,

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.790
so I tried so hard to draw it well...

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.240
They say that you can just fix it later...

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.360
...for the book release, but I can't allow that.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.240
If you can't allow that,
get it in before the deadline.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.740
Someone who can't even get the basics right...

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.290
...doesn't have the right to be contentious.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.240
I know that!

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.800
How many more pages do you have to ink?

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:21.250
Five.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.510
You can't be serious...

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.010
Hurry up and get it done already!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.760
I told you I'd do it, so get off my back!

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.020
Takano...

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.750
She looks like she hasn't been sleeping,

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.400
so shouldn't you try to be a little nicer to her?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.600
Why don't you get to work?

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.480
Yes, sir.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:02.800
Hey, do you think this manga is any good?

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.300
What?

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.480
Is it too late to fix it?

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.720
I don't even know anymore...

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.750
...if I'm writing something good, or if it's just crap.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.520
Of course it's too late.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:18.810
Idiot!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.520
See, your tone...

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.440
I really want to go back and fix it.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.080
Can it and work.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.320
She's really doubting herself.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.330
You should be giving her support!

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.330
Can't you see she needs that?

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:40.870
Takano... I...

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.590
Stop wasting calories.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.940
That's it!

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.340
Uh... I want you to know that
I bought your last volume.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:54.770
What?

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:57.860
Uh... Well, you see...

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.580
I just got into manga publishing,

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:05.070
so now I'm reading everything we publish.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:06.680
Even as a guy, I enjoyed it.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:08.610
So when I heard you had...

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:13.010
...a new volume out this month,
I went out and bought it.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.820
Can't you get them for free at work?

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:20.830
I do, but since I liked it so much,

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.530
I thought I should reward the creator by buying a copy.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.180
Because giving money to Marukawa,

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.380
after Marukawa paid you, makes a lot of sense.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.380
You just realized that?

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.990
I'm an idiot.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:38.780
Anyway, I think your manga is fun to read.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:41.390
So please, you're almost done!

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:45.330
I just wanted to try to cheer you up a bit.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.980
I guess I'm the one who can't tell what she needs.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.600
Even the rookie says so.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.200
Has there even been a mistake in something...

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.060
...where I had OKed the storyboard?

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:03.630
No.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:06.730
Then you don't have to redo it.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:11.280
I talked to the printer,

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.180
and you have an extension until tomorrow morning.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:19.330
So that's who he was yelling at on
the phone on the way over here.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.060
He was negotiating with the printer...

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:27.060
But I was told to have it done by noon today.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.070
We know there's no way you can finish it.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.990
But it's so hard to get them to agree to an extension.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.410
Just so you know,

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.010
things like this lowers your reputation.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:44.830
Got it.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.860
Then hurry up and get it done!

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.860
Yes, sir.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:58.350
I didn't have to cheer her up.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:03.600
Takano was planning on letting her finish properly.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.940
Please paste number forty-one here.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.130
Yes!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:15.840
Uh... How do you paste on the tones?

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:16.570
Huh?

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.360
Well...

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:43.160
I did it!

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.520
I finished the Nikkō Tōshō-gū!

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.100
All right!

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:49.680
Good job!

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.050
Way to go!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.520
Good job.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.550
All right, let's get this to the printer.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:55.460
Okay!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.330
I can't do this anymore.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.410
I'm so tired.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:25.040
I'm so sleepy.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.810
But man, were the people at the printer...

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:30.070
...scary just now when we
handed in the manuscript.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:36.070
So then, once the galley is done,

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.200
I have to check that and then it's good to go.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:42.810
I guess the printers still have a lot of work to do...

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:44.950
...once we hand in the proof.

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:47.960
So I guess...

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:54.060
...they'll be glaring at me again when
I go to hand in the galleys.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:11:01.250
Who knew the morning light
could be this destructive?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.750
We're done.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.620
I'm really glad we got it in, in the end.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.140
And I'm glad you were there.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:18.990
What?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.980
She's not usually one of the hysterical ones,

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.670
but this time she was having
a real hard time getting it out.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.710
I think you gave her back
some of her confidence.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.000
Oh, no...

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:36.750
I'm really sorry I did that.

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:41.380
I wish I had more tact...

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.400
But that's me.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.510
When something's important,
I blurt out exactly what I feel.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.300
Indeed.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:53.800
For you.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.290
Th-Thank you.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.640
I guess even he smiles once in a while.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:04.530
Well, yeah, of course he does.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:08.500
Okay, so why am I getting all nervous?

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.360
It's good to be direct.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:15.630
I think it's a huge compliment to
say that her comic is fun to read.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.460
I-I guess that's fine then...

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:27.570
I might have to rethink my impression of this guy.

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:32.580
He draws out the best from the authors,

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.830
works with them to make something good,

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:37.770
and then those books sell...

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:46.120
He's doing what I dream of doing.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.180
I'm an idiot!

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.890
Why am I getting all nervous?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.960
He's a guy, for chrissake!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:59.840
And I told myself I'm never falling
in love again, with anybody!

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.390
You haven't changed at all.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.340
What do you mean?

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.350
I guess you don't remember me.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:15.230
Oh, yeah.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.060
You mentioned that before, too.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.950
But I think you've got me
confused for someone else.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.610
I'm sure this is the first time we've met.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.830
What are you doing?!

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:33.160
Now maybe you'll remember me...

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:39.110
T-Takano!

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.620
If this is a joke, it isn't funny!

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.210
I'm a man!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.250
A joke?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:57.230
Yeah, I suppose you'd always think of it that way.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.740
Huh?

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:03.190
I thought you'd changed a lot,
but you're just as direct as always.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.110
What are you talking about?

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.320
You said that you loved me.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.110
What?

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:25.090
You said that you loved me.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:26.100
What?

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.720
So what? You rejected me
and now you're pretending...

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.180
...you don't even remember?

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.010
What?

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.060
The galleys should be done now.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.600
I'm going to drop them off at the printer.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.430
You can try to remember while I'm gone.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:40.350
What are you talking about?!

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:41.760
Takano!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.800
My senior year in high-school,

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.110
my parents got a divorce
and my last name changed.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:47.410
Huh?

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.140
My name used to be Saga.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.270
Masamune Saga.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.110
Masamune Saga.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.140
Masamune Saga.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.490
Saga...

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.130
Saga...

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:15.550
We... We're going out, right?

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:16.310
What?

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:20.520
Well, I'm just wondering, because
you never say anything.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.500
Saga

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.170
It couldn't be...

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:25.020
It couldn't be...

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:31.290
Do you...feel anything for me?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.790
He laughed.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:41.550
Why?!

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.130
Was he just...

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.590
...playing with me?!

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.830
Stop right there, Saga!

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:50.230
I mean, Takano!

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.370
So Masamune Saga and Masamune
Takano are one and the same!

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:57.430
He's the first love I've so desperately
expunged from my memories!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.920
Why do I have to run into him
again here of all places?

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:02.730
And why the hell does he have to be my boss?!

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:04.820
Stop right there!

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:07.480
You can't just say whatever the
hell you want and then run away!

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.540
So you thought you'd just
drop this one me, huh?!

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:14.190
You could at least apologize,
after what you've done to me!

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:15.750
What did I do?

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.020
You know!

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:18.180
I did something to you?

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:19.830
Do you see anyone else here?!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.570
Because of that, I...

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:23.370
You're the one who did something to me!

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:24.570
What?

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:26.630
You're the one who roundhouse kicked me,

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.630
and then disappeared the next day!

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.230
Roundhouse kick?

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.310
What is that supposed to mean?

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:37.270
What the fuck?

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:40.140
It must be convenient to
have a selective memory.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.620
You're really terrible.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.460
You must be talking about yourself!

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.150
I mean sure, maybe I was young,
but I really meant what I said.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:50.810
You led me on and then you threw me away!

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:51.890
Excuse me?

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.400
When did I ever do that?

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:57.660
When you laughed when I asked
you how you felt about me!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.020
I don't even remember that!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:03.480
Anyway, that doesn't mean anything.
I was a brat in high-school.

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:06.170
If I laughed, it was probably
to hide my embarrassment.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:10.700
So you thought I was making fun of you,

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.050
and that's why you kicked me and ran away?

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.870
And you've held a grudge for ten years?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:18.800
You...

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.890
...are an idiot.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.810
Damn you.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:25.120
You're the one who was acting like an idiot!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.810
So the mystery is finally solved.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:29.820
So that means that I can seduce you, right?

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:31.040
Huh?

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.830
No matter who I was with,
I could never forget you.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:43.910
I'm going to make you say you love me again.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:45.500
Just you wait.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:49.590
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:54.820
Pain

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:58.020
Calm down.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.670
Just calm down.

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:01.640
What does this mean?

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.810
That I made a colossal misunderstanding?

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:06.570
Could it be...?

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.550
But...

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:15.530
My soul got all twisted and
jaded when he did that.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:18.220
Now he's going to say it was nothing
but a bit of nervous laughter?!

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.560
That was stupid.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:25.000
How did I not notice it was
him from the very start?

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:31.030
But his hair is completely different.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.560
And then it's been ten years!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:34.500
Of course I've forgotten!

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:40.560
If I had noticed, I would've just quit right away.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.840
I couldn't forget you.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.270
What if...

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:55.370
What if what he said is true?

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.790
What if I did misunderstand?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:08.360
Maybe he did...love me?

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.290
Maybe he still does?

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:16.300
Does that mean I can love him again?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:19.550
I was the one who liked him first.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:23.490
Maybe it would be just like in the mangas.

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:27.570
I'd tell him I love him and then
we cut to the happy ending.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.310
Yeah right!

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:32.950
Maybe it was nervous laughter,

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:36.020
but he's the one who did
something ambiguous at that point,

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.320
so he's the one in the wrong!

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:42.880
I'm annoying myself for even letting
something like that influence me!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:44.740
I'm too jaded to accept his
explanation just like that!

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:49.780
No.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.500
This isn't love.

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:54.210
Who could possibly fall in
love with such a guy twice?

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.870
So he thinks he's going to
make me say "I love you?"

00:19:57.870 --> 00:19:59.690
Over my cold, dead body!

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.220
All right, that was the last of it.

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:04.250
Thank you very much.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.660
Thank you.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:15.870
Starting a new job while you move really sucks.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.460
I really don't want to go to work.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.760
That department's really weird, too.

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:25.240
I don't even know what making
manga is about anymore.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:27.020
And then I've got him for a boss.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.020
I can't believe it.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.360
It's supposed to be time
to turn over a new leaf,

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:37.070
but I'm exhausted, body and soul.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:39.830
Huh?

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:42.250
Where did they put the box cutter?

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:46.990
I guess I'll go get some food from the
convenience store while I get one.

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.840
Oh, he must be a neighbor.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:20:59.690
Hello!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:01.530
I'm your new neighbor.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.530
Oh, so you're my new neighbor?

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:15.770
Thump thump thump

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.360
What is Takano doing here?

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:13.120
Don't tell me he's my neighbor!

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.580
Oh, I get it.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.790
You came to confess your love for me.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.500
You sure changed your mind quick.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.050
I'm fine with that.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.490
What are you talking about?!

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:24.050
That is outrageous!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.540
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:32.290
Why does he have to live next to me?

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:33.810
I cannot believe this!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.390
This is bad.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.450
I've gotta move stat!

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:40.580
I'm broke, but that doesn't matter!

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:41.820
Just pull yourself together!

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:44.350
This isn't love, this isn't love...

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:48.960
Under no circumstances is this love!

